.TH "GOREECLOUD-TERMINAL" 1 "21 August 2026"
.SH NAME
goreecloud-terminal \- launch GoreeCloud Terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B goreecloud-terminal
.RI [OPTION]...
[\-\- PROGRAM ARGUMENTS]
.br
.B goreecloud-terminal api
.B status
.br
.B goreecloud-terminal ssh
.RI [OPENSSH_ARGUMENT ...]
.br
.B goreecloud-terminal ssh-tab
.RI [OPENSSH_ARGUMENT ...]
.br
.B goreecloud-terminal workspaces
.br
.B goreecloud-terminal profiles
.RI [WORKSPACE]
.br
.B goreecloud-terminal profile
.I PROFILE
.RI [REMOTE_COMMAND ...]
.br
.B goreecloud-terminal profile-tab
.I PROFILE
.RI [REMOTE_COMMAND ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B goreecloud-terminal
is the canonical command-line launcher for GoreeCloud Terminal.
.PP
For ordinary arguments, it forwards the command line unchanged to the inherited
.B ptyxis
runtime so GoreeCloud can provide a first-party command name without prematurely breaking compatibility-sensitive runtime, helper, packaging, D-Bus, or rollback behavior.
.PP
GoreeCloud Terminal is a GoreeCloud-maintained open-source fork of Ptyxis. The upstream runtime foundation and GPL attribution remain preserved.
.SH LOCAL API
The supported GoreeCloud Terminal API is:
.PP
.nf
goreecloud-terminal api status
.fi
.PP
It returns schema-versioned JSON containing static product, release, identity, Privacy Shield, and Wardveil integration metadata. The API is read-only and local to the CLI. It does not open a network listener, enumerate sessions or profiles, or include terminal contents, commands, credentials, host aliases, or identifiers.
.PP
.B goreecloud-terminal api --help
prints the supported API usage. Unknown API operations fail before the inherited terminal runtime is launched.
.SH SSH WORKFLOWS
The
.B ssh
subcommand opens a new GoreeCloud Terminal window running the system
.BR ssh (1)
client.
.PP
The
.B ssh-tab
subcommand opens the OpenSSH session as a new tab in the existing GoreeCloud Terminal instance.
.PP
Arguments after either subcommand are passed to the system ssh command unchanged. Normal OpenSSH argument ordering therefore applies: command-line options precede the destination and an optional remote command follows it.
.PP
OpenSSH remains responsible for host configuration, host-key verification, authentication, keys, agents, ports, proxy settings, forwarding, and connection policy. GoreeCloud Terminal does not store SSH passwords or private keys and does not replace OpenSSH configuration.
.SH HOST PROFILES AND WORKSPACES
GoreeCloud Terminal may optionally organize standard OpenSSH Host aliases using a local metadata file.
.PP
The default profile file is:
.PP
.nf
$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/goreecloud-terminal/profiles.tsv
.fi
.PP
or, when XDG_CONFIG_HOME is unset:
.PP
.nf
~/.config/goreecloud-terminal/profiles.tsv
.fi
.PP
Each active line contains exactly three TAB-separated fields:
.PP
.nf
WORKSPACE<TAB>PROFILE<TAB>SSH_HOST_ALIAS
.fi
.PP
The profile file is organizational metadata only. It must not replace OpenSSH configuration or contain passwords, private-key material, reusable secrets, port policy, proxy policy, identity-file paths, or authentication policy.
.PP
The
.B workspaces
command lists configured workspace labels once in first-seen order.
.PP
The
.B profiles
command lists PROFILE, WORKSPACE, and SSH_HOST_ALIAS fields. An optional WORKSPACE argument restricts the listing.
.PP
The
.B profile
command resolves PROFILE to its configured OpenSSH Host alias and opens a new window running standard OpenSSH.
.PP
The
.B profile-tab
command performs the same alias resolution but opens the session in a new tab.
.PP
Duplicate profile IDs, malformed rows, aliases containing whitespace, aliases beginning with a hyphen, unknown workspaces, unknown profiles, and missing configuration fail before the terminal runtime is launched.
.SH COMPATIBILITY
The inherited
.B ptyxis
command remains installed during the current migration stage. Existing scripts and workflows may continue using it.
.PP
New GoreeCloud documentation and normal user workflows should prefer
.B goreecloud-terminal
unless a compatibility test specifically requires the inherited command.
.SH OPTIONS
Except for the GoreeCloud subcommands documented above, command-line options and program arguments are passed directly to the
.B ptyxis
runtime. For the inherited option set, see:
.PP
.BR ptyxis (1)
.SH EXAMPLES
Open GoreeCloud Terminal:
.PP
.nf
goreecloud-terminal
.fi
.PP
Read the local API status contract:
.PP
.nf
goreecloud-terminal api status
.fi
.PP
Open a standard OpenSSH session using an OpenSSH Host alias:
.PP
.nf
goreecloud-terminal ssh server-alias
.fi
.PP
Use a non-default OpenSSH port with normal option ordering:
.PP
.nf
goreecloud-terminal ssh -p 2222 server-alias
.fi
.PP
Open a configured GoreeCloud Terminal profile in a new window:
.PP
.nf
goreecloud-terminal profile primary-vps
.fi
.PP
List profiles within one workspace:
.PP
.nf
goreecloud-terminal profiles Infrastructure
.fi
.SH SECURITY
Do not place reusable passwords, private-key material, tokens, or other secrets directly in command-line arguments or GoreeCloud Terminal profile metadata. Standard OpenSSH and operating-system credential controls remain authoritative.
.PP
Workspace labels and aliases may reveal infrastructure organization even when they are not credentials. Protect the profile file as private local configuration.
.SH RELEASE STATUS
The source line identifies Release Candidate 50.2-rc.1. Release Candidate status is not Stable or production approval. See release/status.json and docs/release-readiness.md for the authoritative source acceptance boundary.
.SH PROJECT
GoreeCloud repository:
.br
https://github.com/GoreeCloud/goreecloud-terminal
.PP
Canonical upstream Ptyxis source:
.br
https://gitlab.gnome.org/chergert/ptyxis
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ptyxis (1),
.BR ssh (1),
.BR ssh_config (5)
